Command Description <code>\d</code> List all tables, views, and sequences. <code>\d &lt;table_name&gt;</code> Describe a specific table (columns, types, etc.). <code>\q</code> Exit the psql interactive terminal. <ol> <li> <p>Create a table by executing the following commands in psql: </p><pre><code>   DROP TABLE IF EXISTS worktable;

   CREATE TABLE worktable (col1 INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, col2 TEXT);
</code></pre><p></p> </li> <li> <p>Enable replication for the table so that you can capture changes made to it: </p><pre><code>   ALTER TABLE worktable REPLICA IDENTITY FULL;
</code></pre><p></p> </li> </ol>
